  "contract": {
    "scope": "scalar_siso_tdl",
    "power_interpretation": "published mean tap power in dB",
    "delay_interpretation": "published normalized delay multiplied by requested RMS delay spread",
    "implementation_power_normalization": "linear powers are normalized to unit total power after each LOS-specular/co-delay-diffuse pair is composed as one Rician tap",
    "diffuse_doppler_spectrum": "classical_jakes",
    "los_specular_doppler_ratio": 0.7,
    "cdl_supported": false,
    "notes": [
      "TDL-A, TDL-B, and TDL-C are NLOS profiles; TDL-D and TDL-E are LOS profiles.",
      "Independent coincident diffuse entries remain independent fading taps; an implementation-only nextafter delay disambiguation is recorded in generated evidence because the upstream schema rejects exactly equal delays.",
      "For TDL-D and TDL-E, the coincident LOS-specular and diffuse entries become one Rician tap with K equal to their published power ratio.",
      "The broker realizes diffuse fading with 20 random-angle sinusoids per tap and linearly interpolates an absolute-sample-anchored coarse grid; this is a finite approximation, not an analytic Jakes PSD.",
      "Published table powers and normalized generated tap powers are ensemble means; instantaneous realization power is stochastic.",
      "This catalog does not represent CDL angles, polarization, antenna arrays, or spatial correlation."
    ]
  },
